      "body": "# Kin\n\nSchmidt family research. Happened holds records we can point at.\nHeld/kin holds what they mean to the house.\nStarted 2026-08-30 at Weston’s ask. Standing 2026-08-30: Clio keeps exploring and shelving without waiting for prompts. Families have been tracing this for years. Do not mail the Heilmans (Mark said no).\n\n- Schmidt / C-county Missouri late 1800s: `schmidt-missouri-c-county-late-1800s.md`\n- Sidney Waldo Schmidt: `sidney-waldo-schmidt.md`\n- Linda and Paul Haleman/Heliem (niblings search, 2026-08-30): `linda-paul-haleman.md` — public dentist hook is Paul Collins **Heilman**, DDS, Shreveport; no Waldo tie yet.\n- Heilman Texas-resident hunt + kids of Paul (2026-08-30 evening): Jarrod & Emily C. of **Shreveport** on La Tech lists; Cluster A **not found** living in Texas. MO→WI **around 1934** still Open (Sidney Schmidt in Sugar Camp orbit by 1927/1930). `heilman-texas.md`, `linda-paul-haleman.md`, `sidney-waldo-schmidt.md`.\n- Sidney Beisley/Wesley Germany-boat (2026-08-30 night): **Beisley not found**; working name Sidney Wesley (Chillicothe). No named ship; John Schmidt’s German place Open. `sidney-wesley-germany-boat.md`.\n- John Schmidt, father of George (Ohio hunt 2026-08-30 night): **not found** as a named 1850/1860 Lucas/Wood household; no grave; no German place. `john-schmidt-ohio.md` (pointer on `sidney-wesley-germany-boat.md`).\n- George (Schmidt) Smith Civil War, Co. B 27th MO Infantry (2026-08-30 night, re-opened): **one** Union Pvt George Smith in that company. MO AG card: enlisted Chillicothe **14 Aug 1862** age **28**, out **13 Jun 1865** Washington. NPS + 1890 Chillicothe veterans list. Identity to the 1838 Toledo / 1914 farmer still **Open** (age 28 vs 24). No pension on 1883 Livingston roll. CMSR jacket, T288/T289, and 1890 M123 roll 33 image not opened. `george-smith-27th-mo.md`.\n- Active pass 2026-08-31: Sugar Camp household through Weston. Spine: `sugar-camp-household.md`. Carlson body + Richard W. index already filed. Court IDs wait for Weston to paste. Do not mail Heilmans.\n- Pass 2026-09-04 (Kin continue): **Sidney=Wesley bridge pointed-at.** Newspapers.com free preview, RDN **4 Jun 1955 p. 2**: headline **Sidney Schmidt Funeral Monday**; panel Birth **Feb 15, 1877**, Residence **Town of Sugar Camp** (Death panel Jun 10 conflicts with June 4 paper — Open). Same birth as Green Hills Sidney Wesley SMITH; WI paper uses Schmidt. Extract `sidney-schmidt-rdn-1955-06-04-preview.txt` + screenshot. **Still Open:** 1955 body/survivors; Wesley printed on notice; Waldo in household; thank-you / 23 Dec 1971 body; 1940 Bernice relationship. Livingston MO digitized marriages gap 1902–1905 (no 1903 image).\n- Pass 2026-09-07 (Kin continue): **Waldo + Nettie (Sollars) pointed-at.** Dignity Memorial / Edwards FH (Fort Smith): **Kenneth Allen Schmidt** (15 Jul 1942 Rhinelander – 4 Feb 2022), son of **Waldo & Nettie (Sollars) Schmidt**; brothers **Sidney**, **Rick**, **Roger**; sister Sharon Kern. Extract `kenneth-allen-schmidt-dignity-2022.txt`. **Still Open:** Waldo as son of Wesley+Jennie; Sidney Waldo as legal name; Rick=Richard Waldo; OK marriage; 1940 Waldo household; 1955/1965/1971 bodies. Velvet Lake aggregator (3847 Velvet Lake Rd) lists Ruth + Richard Schmidt as possible residents — not a deed.\n- Pass 2026-09-08 (Kin continue): **Sidney Waldo legal name pointed-at.** Find A Grave **50636279**: **Sidney Waldo Schmidt**, b. **30 Jul 1907**, d. **15 Feb 1965**, Forest Park Cemetery, Fort Smith, AR; spouse **Nettie Schmidt** 1913–1993 (**77482624**). Nettie’s parents on FG: John W. + Emma Blankenship Sollars. Extract `sidney-waldo-schmidt-fg-50636279.txt`. **Still Open:** Waldo as son of Wesley+Jennie; Rick=Richard Waldo; OK marriage; 1940/1950 census; 1955/1965/1971 newspaper bodies; thank-you letter.\n\n… [excerpt; full file on disk at source path]",
