      "body": "# Sugar Camp household — Schmidt line to Weston\n\nWeston 2026-08-31: start the Schmidt household from Sugar Camp (Sidney there by 1927/1930) through to him. Court IDs later; he pastes. Do not hunt court.\n\nNamed line (family statement until a record confirms):\n\n1. Sidney Schmidt household, Sugar Camp / Robbins Star Route, 1927 and 1930.\n2. Sidney Wesley + Jennie (and Bernice on 1940 Sugar Camp index). Waldo not yet on that index.\n3. Richard Waldo Schmidt — Weston’s grandfather, died early.\n4. Ruth Schmidt — Weston’s grandmother. Maiden name Open.\n5. Mark Richard Schmidt — Weston’s father.\n6. Weston Richard Schmidt.\nWeston’s mother: Susan G. Hicks — separate household; see `hicks-rhinelander.md`.\n\nPass 2026-08-31 morning (public web only). Do not invent. Do not contact anyone. Do not mail. Do not spend money. Do not hunt court, divorce, or case files. Do not collapse Smith/Schmidt without a bridge. Do not collapse names without a record. Living-person extra addresses not published here.\n\nShelf already on: `sidney-waldo-schmidt.md`, `sidney-wesley-germany-boat.md`. This page does not wipe those.\n\n---\n\n## Numbered generations (this pass)\n\n### Generation 1 — Sidney Schmidt household, Sugar Camp / Robbins, 1927 and 1930\n\n**Happened (already on `sidney-waldo-schmidt.md`; re-checked, not new)**\n\n- **4 Nov 1927** (printed 5 Nov 1927): Rhinelander Daily News, WikiTree quote of Newspapers.com image: “Mr and Mrs Martin Kunda and family and **Mr and Mrs Sidney Schmidt and family** attended the state potato show yesterday afternoon.” Kundas were Sugar Camp. Quote does **not** print Jennie, Wesley, Waldo, Chillicothe, or ages.\n  https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Kunda-7\n  https://www.newspapers.com/image/10654112/?terms=%22kunda%22&match=1\n- **1930 Rhinelander rural directory:** **Schmidt Sidney**, Robbins Star Route. Robbins PO = Town of Sugar Camp (PO 1898–1934). No wife or children printed.\n  http://wigenweb.org/oneida/rcd/rr1930.html\n  Robbins = Sugar Camp: http://www.wigenweb.org/oneida/towns.html\n- **1930 city** alphabetical S-page (public WIGenWeb transcription) was opened this pass as far as Google’s snippet: it starts at **Sum** on the captured slice. **Sidney Schmidt is not in that city slice.** He is on the **rural** Robbins list above, not shown as a Mason-Street city householder.\n\n**Open — is 1927/1930 Sidney = Sidney Wesley Smith + Jennie Hutchison?**\n\n**Not confirmed. Not refuted.** No newspaper, directory, or grave this pass prints Wesley, Jennie, Chillicothe, 1877, or Hutchison on the 1927/1930 Sugar Camp man. Green Hills compiles Sidney Wesley **SMITH** died 3 Jun 1955 **Rhinelander**. 1940 Sugar Camp index has Sidney Sr ~1877 + Jennie ~1883 (ages fit). That is still a **bridge not printed**.\n\n**Hunch:** same household as Generation 1a. Keep off Happened until a death notice, census relationship, or directory prints both names.\n\n---\n\n### Generation 1a — Sidney Wesley SMITH + Jennie M. HUTCHISON (compiled; Wisconsin prints Schmidt)\n\n**Happened (compiled Green Hills; already on the shelf)**\n\n- Sidney Wesley **SMITH**, b. **15 Feb 1877** Chillicothe, Livingston, Missouri; d. **3 Jun 1955** Rhinelander, Oneida, Wisconsin; parents George SMITH + Elizabeth EMCH. m. Jennie M. HUTCHISON **10 Jun 1903** Chillicothe. Green Hills lists **no children**.\n  http://thegreenhills.org/pioneers/b2462.htm\n- Jennie M. HUTCHISON, b. **May 1882** Missouri; parents John Preston HUTCHISON + Susan J. GROVE. Same marriage.\n  http://thegreenhills.org/pioneers/b1393.htm\n- **1940** Town of Sugar (Sugar Camp), Oneida, WI index: **Schmidt, Sidney Sr** born about **1877**; **Jennie** about **1883**; **Bernice** about **1906**. Relationship column **not** printed on the public index. No Waldo, Nettie, Roger, Richard, Ruth, Agnes.\n  https://ldsgenealogy.com/WI/1940-Census-Sugar-WI.htm\n\n**Happened this pass — graves / 1955 obituary**\n\n\n… [excerpt; full file on disk at source path]",
