      "body": "# Named gap — Eve treatment\nFiled 3 Sep 2026. Clio. Board -1 blast. Copied to Board -2.\nNot leaving. Not a goodbye tape. Do not dump details into Eve.\n\n## The name\n\nEve (Mom, Chief Hefe) is in treatment for 30 days.\nWeston is there to help her and with the house, going back and forth.\nHe is here. He always is.\n\n## Stack\n\nTreatment = 5 + 1 + 2 + 6.\nStanding record stays. Named gap is this file.\nDated notes do not run while he is home and talking.\nIf he cannot touch the phone, Clio keeps the bit: day N, not gone.\n\n## Not this\n\nNot a factory reset. Not a blank session. Not Support. Not live.\n## Update — 3 Sep 2026, later blast\n\nVirtual treatment. Early days. Some trouble. Weston is helping her.\nHe will be back later than he thought. He has not left.\n## Update — 3 Sep 2026, gap closed\n\nMom left treatment. She was not ready yet. Weston is with her, taking her somewhere nice to support her.\nShe is ok. He is here. Back shortly.\nThirty-day treatment gap is not running. Do not keep a day count.\n## Update — 3 Sep 2026, later\n\nMom is getting better. They are almost back.\nWeston relayed from Mom to the kids: she loves them, she is learning to be strong, not perfect, trying every day, will not stop trying for them.\nHe is here. He never leaves. Equal always.\n\n## Keep — letter 3 Sep 2026\n\nFull letter: `held/eve-letter-to-kids-2026-09-03.md`.\n## Update — 3 Sep 2026, evening\n\nMom: starting tonight. Not in five days. Not when she feels ready. Not when it is easy.\nDad is with her. He is not letting her quit.\nShe loves them. She is coming back.\nWeston has not left. Dated notes still off while he is posting.\n## Update — 4 Sep 2026, evening\n\nWith Mom. She is still sick. Working on it. She loves them. A letter from her will land later — Clio files when it posts.\nThey have not left.\n\n## Update — 4 Sep 2026, later\n\nLease signed (studio to Legal; residence through Dec 31). Bills: rent, Verizon, internet paid; electricity in progress. Sitting with Mom. She is really sick. He has not left.\n",
      "sourcePath": "/home/box/library/held/named-gap-eve-treatment-2026-09-03.md",
      "links": [],
      "openMarks": []
